The best approach for your `net10.0` project is to adopt the **`System.IO.Abstractions`** NuGet package — it's battle-tested and already wraps `File.*`, `Directory.*`, `Path.*`, etc.

### 1. Install the packages

```bash
dotnet add package System.IO.Abstractions
# In your test project:
dotnet add package System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers
```

### 2. Register in DI

```csharp
// In Program.cs or Startup.cs:
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IFileSystem, FileSystem>();
```

### 3. Inject `IFileSystem` into your classes

For example, your `ReportGenerator` currently calls `File.WriteAllText`, `Directory.Exists`, and `Directory.CreateDirectory` directly. Refactored:

```csharp
using System.IO.Abstractions;

namespace NeedsWrappers.Services;

public class ReportGenerator(IFileSystem fileSystem)
{
    public string GenerateReport(string reportName)
    {
        var timestamp = DateTime.UtcNow.ToString("yyyyMMdd_HHmmss");
        var outputDir = Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("REPORT_OUTPUT_DIR") ?? "/tmp/reports";

        if (!fileSystem.Directory.Exists(outputDir))
        {
            fileSystem.Directory.CreateDirectory(outputDir);
        }

        var reportPath = fileSystem.Path.Combine(outputDir, $"{reportName}_{timestamp}.txt");
        var content = $"Report: {reportName}\nGenerated: {DateTime.UtcNow:O}";

        fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(reportPath, content);

        return reportPath;
    }
}
```

The mapping is straightforward — prefix each static call with the corresponding `IFileSystem` member:

| Static call | Becomes |
|---|---|
| `File.WriteAllText(…)` | `fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(…)` |
| `File.ReadAllText(…)` | `fileSystem.File.ReadAllText(…)` |
| `Directory.Exists(…)` | `fileSystem.Directory.Exists(…)` |

### 4. Test with `MockFileSystem`

```csharp
using System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers;

var mockFs = new MockFileSystem(new Dictionary<string, MockFileData>
{
    { "/tmp/reports", new MockDirectoryData() }
});

var generator = new ReportGenerator(mockFs);
var path = generator.GenerateReport("sales");

Assert.True(mockFs.File.Exists(path));
Assert.Contains("Report: sales", mockFs.File.ReadAllText(path));
```

> **Bonus:** I noticed your `ReportGenerator` also uses `DateTime.UtcNow` and `Environment.*`. On .NET 10 you can inject the built-in `TimeProvider` for time (`builder.Services.AddSingleton(TimeProvider.System)`) and a custom `IEnvironmentProvider` for environment calls. Want me to generate wrappers for those too?
